     wwaattcchh — periodically execute a command and display its output

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     wwaattcchh [--cceellwwxx] [--ss _s_e_c_o_n_d_s] _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_a_r_g _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwaattcchh utility periodically executes and displays the output of
     _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.  Differences between successive runs can be highlighted.

     The options are as follows:

     --cc      Highlight changed characters.

     --ee      Pause updating if _c_o_m_m_a_n_d exits with a non-zero exit code.

     --ll      Highlight changed lines.

     --ss _s_e_c_o_n_d_s
             Set the interval between updates to _s_e_c_o_n_d_s.  The default is 1
             second.

     --ww      Highlight changed words.

     --xx      Pass _c_o_m_m_a_n_d to execl(3) instead of sshh --cc, for different quoting
             and shell escaping behaviour.

IINNTTEERRAACCTTIIVVEE CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
     Certain characters cause immediate action by wwaattcchh.  These are:

     ⟨SSppaaccee⟩
             Run _c_o_m_m_a_n_d again.

     ⟨PPaaggee DDoowwnn⟩
             Scroll down a screenful.

     ⟨PPaaggee UUpp⟩
             Scroll up a screenful.

     [[ | ⟨lleefftt aarrrrooww⟩
             Scroll left by one column.

     ]] | ⟨rriigghhtt aarrrrooww⟩
             Scroll right by one column.

     cc       Highlight changed characters.

     ee       Pause command executions if the command exits with a non-zero
             exit code.

     gg       Scroll to top.

     HH       Scroll left half a screen.

     hh | ??   Display a summary of the commands (help screen).

     JJ       Scroll down half a screen.

     jj | ⟨ddoowwnn aarrrrooww⟩
             Scroll down one line.

     KK       Scroll up half a screen.

     kk | ⟨uupp aarrrrooww⟩
             Scroll up one line.

     LL       Scroll right half a screen.

     ll       Highlight changed lines.

     rr       Display information about resource utilization.

     ss       Change the update interval.

     pp       Pause or resume command executions.  ⟨SSppaaccee⟩ can be used while
             paused.

     ww       Highlight changed words.

     qq       Quit wwaattcchh.

